      "title": "Pure life pays while the covered person lives",
      "narration": "David compares annuity income options using the same amount of money. Pure life, also called straight life or life only, pays for his covered lifetime and stops at his death, without an added refund or guaranteed payment period. If he dies soon after income begins, a beneficiary does not automatically receive the amount he originally paid. If he lives much longer, lifetime payments continue under the promise. Compared with otherwise similar options that add survivor or refund guarantees, pure life generally provides a larger initial periodic payment. That comparison assumes the same funding and comparable contract terms. A larger check comes with a different protection pattern.",
