      "title": "Life with a certain period protects two possibilities",
      "narration": "Now assume David chooses life income with ten years certain. If he dies after exactly four years of payments, the remaining six years of guaranteed payments continue to the designated recipient under the option. If he is still living after ten years, his life payments continue. The ten-year period is a minimum payment guarantee, not a limit on his life income. Compare that with a ten-year period-certain-only option. That option pays for the stated ten years and ends even if David remains alive. The words life with change the result. Read whether the promise lasts for a lifetime, a defined period, or the longer of those two.",
