      "title": "Refund options protect a stated minimum total",
      "narration": "A life-with-refund option pays lifetime income and adds a stated minimum-total protection if the annuitant dies early. Assume one hundred thousand dollars is the contract's refundable purchase amount and thirty thousand dollars has been paid when David dies. With no other adjustment, seventy thousand dollars remains under that refund promise. A cash-refund option pays that amount in one sum. An installment-refund option continues the stated installments until the required total has been paid. Those beneficiary installments do not automatically last for the beneficiary's lifetime. If David instead lives long enough to receive more than the purchase amount, his life income still continues under the contract.",
