      "title": "For two lives, check the survivor’s percentage",
      "narration": "Rosa and David want income to continue while either of them lives. A joint-and-survivor option can provide that protection. Suppose the stated payment is two thousand dollars each month while both live, with seventy-five percent continuing to the survivor. After the triggering death, the survivor receives fifteen hundred dollars monthly under those assumptions. A full-survivor option would continue the stated full amount; other percentages produce different results. The words joint or two lives alone do not establish the continuation amount. Read whose death triggers a reduction and whether payments continue to the last survivor. That is different from an arrangement expressly payable only while both people remain alive.",
