      "title": "Match the guarantee to the household’s priority",
      "narration": "Rosa asks whether the highest available initial payment is always the best choice. It is not. Compare the need for income during one or two lifetimes, a minimum amount for beneficiaries, available cash elsewhere and the effect of inflation. A fixed dollar payment can buy less as prices rise, even when every promised payment arrives. The choice also depends on the specific contract, because income elections and later access may be restricted. For an exam, identify what is guaranteed first: a life, a number of years, a minimum total or a payment size. Then follow the stated death or survival event to determine which payments stop, continue or change.",
